From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:27:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: shared chunk packets

performance.network.shared-chunk-packets (off by default). Players sent
the same chunk in the same pass of the player chunk loader of a world
share one ClientboundLevelChunkWithLightPacket instead of one each. Off,
the window is never opened: each hunk is one static boolean read or one
field compared with the current thread, and every packet is built for
its player as before.

- ServerLevel: btc$chunkPackets, the packets built during the pass
  (dev.btc.core.performance.SharedChunkPackets), empty outside it.
- RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader#tick: the pass over the players of the
  world is the window - opened before, closed in a finally. The option
  is read once so that the window opened is the window closed.
- PlayerChunkSender#sendChunk: inside the window, and only for a player
  Anti-Xray does not rewrite the packet for, the packet comes from the
  window. A send from elsewhere (refreshChunk, a plugin, another thread
  under parallel world ticking) builds its own.
- LevelChunk#markUnsaved: a chunk that changes inside the window is
  dropped from it. Plugins run between two players of the pass
  (PlayerChunkLoadEvent, PlayerChunkUnloadEvent, what a ticket update
  fires): the next player is sent a packet built after the change.

What is shared is the packet object; each connection still encodes it
into its own buffer, which is where CraftEngine and packetevents rewrite
it. Nothing is kept past the pass. A change that does not mark its chunk
as to be saved is not seen.

Idea: the chunk packet cache SteelMC empties each tick
(player/chunk_sender.rs) and Minestom's CachedPacket, as read in
research/chunks-pumpkin.md (G1). BTC addition; nothing is ported.

diff --git a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/player/RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader.java b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/player/RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader.java
index 45c927417d34ddd48c92116efd9b5777bfc52e35..f7140ab530bdffcaca3ca19dfe69aadac8bb66e2 100644
--- a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/player/RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader.java
+++ b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/chunk_system/player/RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader.java
@@ -305,6 +305,9 @@ public final class RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader {
 
     public void tick() {
         TickThread.ensureTickThread("Cannot tick player chunk loader async");
+        final boolean btc$shared = dev.btc.core.config.BTCCoreConfig.networkSharedChunkPackets; // BTCCore - performance.network.shared-chunk-packets: read once, the window opened is the window closed
+        if (btc$shared) this.world.btc$chunkPackets.open(); // BTCCore - performance.network.shared-chunk-packets: players sent the same chunk in this pass share its packet
+        try { // BTCCore - performance.network.shared-chunk-packets
         long currTime = System.nanoTime();
         for (final ServerPlayer player : new java.util.ArrayList<>(this.world.players())) {
             final PlayerChunkLoaderData loader = ((ChunkSystemServerPlayer)player).moonrise$getChunkLoader();
@@ -315,6 +318,9 @@ public final class RegionizedPlayerChunkLoader {
             loader.update(); // can't invoke plugin logic
             loader.updateQueues(currTime);
         }
+        } finally { // BTCCore - performance.network.shared-chunk-packets: nothing is kept past the pass, so a block changed later is never in a packet built earlier
+            if (btc$shared) this.world.btc$chunkPackets.close();
+        }
     }
 
     public static final class PlayerChunkLoaderData {
